          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "type": "any"
        }
      ],
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Behavior\n\n## Implemented behavior\n\nedgeLegality resolves the class key, checks kinds and counts matching incoming/outgoing relationships. The graph validator diagnoses loaded invalid relationships, and mutation paths can reject illegal new edges. Intergraph edge references preserve ownership on participating Declarations.\n\n## Known gaps\n\nBefore default edge classes load there may be no rule to apply. This is registry availability, not proof that any authored relationship is valid. Browser reconnect/drag behavior requires its own smoke test.\n\n## Open decisions\n\nNo additional decision is required to describe the behavior above. Changes to that contract require an explicit task; implementation gaps are not implied approvals.\n\n## Evidence\n\nSource (twilite repository):\n- `components/GraphEditor/utils/edgeLegality.js`\n- `components/GraphEditor/utils/interGraphEdge.js`\n- `components/GraphEditor/validators/validateGraphInvariants.js`\n\nFocused tests (twilite repository):\n- `tests/edgeLegality.test.js`\n- `tests/edgeEndpointResolution.test.js`\n- `tests/interGraphEdge.test.js`\n\nThese pointers identify evidence to inspect. Structural validation does not prove runtime or browser behavior."
        },
        "interfaceContract": {
          "version": 1,
          "receivesViewContent": true
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "primitive-edge",
          "nodeId": "edge-behavior"
        }
      }
    },
